      "body": "Fixes #4486 (task 6439).\n\n`ReplicationTracker::accept` verified that each payload line decodes as a journal entry, but never checked the payload's own journal header — a signed Snapshot with no header, a foreign world's header, a mismatched header version, or a duplicate header advanced the verified cursor over a journal `WorldCore::restore` refuses.\n\n## Change (`pkgs/id/src/world/replication.rs` only)\n- New `ReplicationError::InvalidJournalHeader`.\n- `validate_payload_journal_header`, called from `accept` in the Snapshot and Tail arms before any state changes:\n  - **Snapshot:** first entry must be exactly one `Created` header whose `world_id` and `version` equal the envelope's `world_id` and `header_version`; any later `Created` is refused; an empty snapshot is a missing header.\n  - **Tail:** a tail starting at the chain base carries journal entry 0 itself, so its first entry may be that same matching header; any other `Created` in a tail is a second header mid-journal and is refused.\n  - Every refusal leaves tracker state unchanged (validation runs before the chain/cursor mutation).\n- Regression test `snapshot_and_tail_payloads_must_carry_the_journals_own_header` covers all five packet cases — missing header, foreign-world header, payload version mismatch, duplicate header, Created in Tail — asserting the cursor does not move on refusal.\n- The header-bump rebase test now carries a version-2 header in its version-2 snapshot payload (previously it reused the version-1 fixture, which the new contract correctly refuses).\n\nOut of scope per the packet: envelope `header_version` lower bound (#4471), references.rs (#4454/#4455), network/durable replica work.\n\n## Tests\n- Laptop, from `pkgs/id`: `cargo test --lib world::replication` — **11 passed, 0 failed** (includes existing round-trip, rebase, gap/fork/replay, and tamper tests).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796240240&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=4550&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F4550&signature=fa477a41dbf04daee02a4565001f6e0af122dcba869504812eec189a6f4112a9\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/4550?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
